    <p class="form-text">
        <?= I18N::translate('A record that belongs to no line — an ancestor above them all, or a branch that was numbered and then died out — is written “GS/” followed by the path itself. The portal reads those too, and they are what lets it reach the deepest ancestors.') ?>
    </p>
    <p class="form-text">
        <?= I18N::translate('The oblique is optional when nothing follows it, so “24” and “24/” both mean the head of line 24. Where a record carries both a bare number and one with an oblique, the second is used — a bare two-digit number is also what an older numbering looks like once it reaches two digits.') ?>
    </p>
    <p class="form-text">
        <?= I18N::translate('“GS” with nothing after it is the progenitor — the one person every number in the archive descends from, and the only way to write him.') ?>
    </p>
    <p class="form-text">
        <?= I18N::translate('Three things are not in the number itself and have to be kept here. All three are shipped with the values the family already uses, and all three are family news rather than software: leave a box empty to keep using what the module was built with.') ?>
    </p>

    <div class="row mb-3">
        <label class="col-sm-3 col-form-label" for="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_LINES ?>">
            <?= I18N::translate('Lines') ?>
        </label>
        <div class="col-sm-9">
            <textarea class="form-control font-monospace" rows="8" id="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_LINES ?>" name="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_LINES ?>" spellcheck="false"><?= e($sack_lines === '' ? $sack_lines_default : $sack_lines) ?></textarea>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('One line per entry, “number = prefix”. The prefix is what the line’s number stands for at the start of every path in it, which is why two people in different lines still have a common ancestor. “GS” needs no entry — it stands for nothing, because a GS number is already the whole path.') ?>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-3">
        <label class="col-sm-3 col-form-label" for="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_MARRIAGES ?>">
            <?= I18N::translate('Marriages within the family') ?>
        </label>
        <div class="col-sm-9">
            <textarea class="form-control font-monospace" rows="10" id="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_MARRIAGES ?>" name="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_MARRIAGES ?>" spellcheck="false"><?= e($sack_marriages === '' ? $sack_marriages_default : $sack_marriages) ?></textarea>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('One line per entry, “number = number”. The children of such a couple are filed under the right-hand number only, so the left-hand parent’s descent is invisible in the children’s numbers — this is what tells the calculation about it. Put a “!” after the left-hand number where that partner is the one who married in. A “#” starts a note.') ?>
            </div>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('Getting this wrong makes relationships wrong rather than absent, so it is worth checking a known pair afterwards. A row that names a line which does not exist is ignored.') ?>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-3">
        <label class="col-sm-3 col-form-label" for="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_BRANCHES ?>">
            <?= I18N::translate('Branches') ?>
        </label>
        <div class="col-sm-9">
            <textarea class="form-control font-monospace" rows="12" id="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_BRANCHES ?>" name="<?= SackNumbers::SETTING_BRANCHES ?>" spellcheck="false"><?= e($sack_branches === '' ? $sack_branches_default : $sack_branches) ?></textarea>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('One line per entry, “lines = name”. The lines are a range — “8-14” — or a single number, and “GS” and “HS” are heads of their own. This is what the portal shows under a member’s number on their record: a member says which branch they come from, not which line number they were filed under.') ?>
            </div>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('A name may be followed by “|” and the same name in another language, each one tagged with it: “Zweig Cleve | en: Cleve Branch”. The portal shows a member the name in the language they are reading it in. A language with no name of its own gets the first one, so a branch written in one language is shown to everybody rather than to nobody.') ?>
            </div>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('A number written without an oblique gets no branch, on purpose: a bare two-digit number is also what the older numbering looks like, and naming the wrong branch is worse than naming none.') ?>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-3">
        <label class="col-sm-3 col-form-label" for="<?= PortalApiModule::SETTING_REMEMBER_DAYS ?>">
            <?= I18N::translate('Let members stay signed in (days)') ?>
        </label>
        <div class="col-sm-9">
            <input class="form-control" type="number" min="0" max="<?= RememberedDevices::MAX_DAYS ?>" id="<?= PortalApiModule::SETTING_REMEMBER_DAYS ?>" name="<?= PortalApiModule::SETTING_REMEMBER_DAYS ?>" value="<?= e($remember_days) ?>">
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('The session ends when the browser closes, so a member who opens the portal once a month types their password every time. With this set, the login screen offers “stay signed in” and that device is let back in without one until the days run out.') ?>
            </div>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('%s switches it off: no offer is made, and any device already remembered stops being let in. 30 is a reasonable figure for a family whose members read the portal on their own telephones.', '0') ?>
            </div>
            <div class="form-text">
                <?= I18N::translate('It is a real key kept on a real device. Whoever picks up an unlocked telephone is that member, without a password — so this is a decision about your family’s telephones, not about the portal. Signing out ends it on that device, and resetting a password ends it everywhere.') ?>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-3">
        <div class="offset-sm-3 col-sm-9">
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">
                <?= view('icons/save') ?>
                <?= I18N::translate('save') ?>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <?= csrf_field() ?>
</form>
